---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import BrandParticles from '../components/BrandParticles.astro';
import { company, site, power, network, compute } from '../data/site';
---

<Content
  title={`About ${company.full} — the data center arm of ${company.parent}`}
  description={`${company.name} is the AI data center business of ${company.parent}. One campus today: ${site.acresRounded} in ${site.name}, across three tracts, with a ${site.powerOn} for first compute.`}
  kicker={`About ${company.name}`}
  heading={`${company.name} is the data center arm of ${company.parent}.`}
  lede={`A founder-led venture developing a single Oklahoma campus with three complementary activities: data-center services, inverter and battery assembly, and solar and storage development. Each is at a different stage, and this page tries to be exact about which.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Site', value: site.designation, note: `${site.name}, ${site.county}` },
    { label: 'Land', value: `${site.acres} acres`, note: 'Three tracts, owner-reported', count: true },
    { label: 'Service', value: power.service, note: 'Shared across Buildings A, B and C', tone: 'gold' },
    { label: 'First compute', value: site.powerOn, note: `${compute.gpus} GPUs planned`, tone: 'signal' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="what" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">What we do</span></p>
    <h2 id="what">We build AI data centers starting from the power, not the rendering</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>
          {company.name} develops and operates AI data center capacity. The company has
          one site: {site.designation}, {site.acres} acres at {site.address} in
          {' '}{site.county}, Oklahoma. The first compute phase is
          {' '}{compute.systems}, on a {site.powerOn}. Which building takes the first
          installation is not yet confirmed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most operators start with a site plan and then go looking for electrons. This
          one started from the opposite end: the parcel was bought with an electrical
          service and three buildings already standing on it. What that buys is a
          starting point, not a finished data center — Buildings A, B and C have no
          established fit-out or commissioning status, and the usable IT capacity behind
          that service follows an engineering review rather than an arithmetic
          conversion of the service rating.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Company</dt><dd>{company.full}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Parent</dt><dd>{company.parent}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Sites</dt><dd>{site.designation} — {site.name}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Land</dt><dd>{site.acres} acres across three tracts</dd></div>
        <div><dt>First capacity</dt><dd>{site.powerOn}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Legal entity</dt><dd><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: registered entity name, state of incorporation, and formation date]</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Headquarters</dt><dd><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: corporate office address, if different from the site]</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="parentage" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">{company.parent}</span></p>
    <h2 id="parentage">Why the parentage changes the economics</h2>

    <p>
      {company.parent} builds LFP battery cabinets. {company.name} is its data center
      business, and {site.manufacturing.buildings} buildings of
      {' '}{site.manufacturing.sqftEach.toLocaleString()} sq ft each are planned on Tract 1 for
      {' '}{site.manufacturing.scope.toLowerCase()}.
    </p>
    <p>
      The argument for that adjacency is a sizing argument rather than a branding one: if
      storage reaches a site closer to what it costs to build, more of it makes economic
      sense there. We have not evidenced that advantage yet, and it is not a claim this
      page will make until it can be:
      {' '}<span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: documented related-party equipment cost, warranty and service obligations before any manufacturer-cost or savings claim is published]</span>.
      The planned scope uses purchased cells and components; it is not lithium-ion cell
      fabrication and not a commissioned production line.
    </p>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Land</h3>
        <p>{site.acres} acres in {site.county}, across three tracts. {site.ownership}; the owning entity is being documented.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Power</h3>
        <p>{power.service}, shared across Buildings A, B and C from Building C. {power.allocation}.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Storage</h3>
        <p>{power.storage}. {power.storageNote}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Network</h3>
        <p>{network.service} from {network.provider}, planned. {network.status}.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">
      Detail on the parent company that a counterparty will reasonably ask for —
      {' '}<span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: {company.parent} founding date, ownership structure, manufacturing locations, and product range]</span>
      {' '}and <span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: whether {company.name} is a subsidiary, a division, or a separate entity under common ownership — and which entity owns the land, leases the equipment, signs customer contracts and would issue any securities]</span>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <BrandParticles />

  <section aria-labelledby="how" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">How we publish</span></p>
    <h2 id="how">Two rules about what appears on this site</h2>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Real photographs or nothing</h3>
        <p>
          Every image on this site is a photograph of this site. Where a photograph has
          not been taken yet, you get an empty frame that says so and describes what
          belongs there. No stock library, no rendered hall, no borrowed data center
          interior. It costs us some polish and it saves you a site visit that turns into
          a disappointment.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>No invented numbers</h3>
        <p>
          Every figure on these pages comes from the owner-confirmed site record, or is
          arithmetic on figures from it with the working shown. Anything we do not know —
          a rack density, a PUE, a price, an SLA — is printed as a visible placeholder
          instead of a plausible number. There are a lot of them, and that is the point.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="pull">
      <p>We would rather show you our gaps now than defend them at contract.</p>
      <p>
        If a competing proposal quotes you a PUE, a tier and a price for a site that has
        not been energised, ask which of those three is measured.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="people" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">People</span></p>
    <h2 id="people">Who you would be dealing with</h2>

    <p>
      <span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: leadership — names, roles, and relevant operating background, for {company.name} and for {company.parent}]</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: who is on site at {site.name}, and whether the site is staffed during construction and after power-on]</span>
    </p>

    <figure class="photo">
      <div class="photo__frame">
        <svg class="photo__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="2.5" y="6" width="19" height="14" rx="2" />
          <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3.5" />
          <path d="M8.5 6l1.4-2.2h4.2L15.5 6" />
          <path d="M3 3l18 18" />
        </svg>
        <p class="photo__state">Photograph not taken yet</p>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>[PHOTO NEEDED]</b> The team on the parcel, and the {company.parent}
        manufacturing floor where the LFP cabinets are built. Both are real places that
        can be photographed; neither has been photographed for this site yet.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="talk" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">05</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Next</span></p>
    <h2 id="talk">Come and look at it</h2>
    <p>
      The site is at {site.address}. If you are evaluating capacity for
      {' '}{site.powerOn} or later, the fastest way to test everything on these pages is
      to stand on the parcel and look at the transformer.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/site">See {site.designation}</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
